   Well, it seems like it sort-of works. Before releasing it to general 
scrutiny, though, I have a few questions for source gurus:

   (1) Are there /any/ monster types that can't wear rings? I see that
polymorphing into a long worm leaves your rings on left and right "scale 
gaps," and even fog clouds have "left swirl" and "right swirl."  I'm 
asking because I want to consider any cases where polymorphing a monster
should cause its rings to fall off.

   (2) I imagine that uniques and shopkeepers shouldn't be allowed to wear 
certain rings; for example, shopkeepers shouldn't wear =oTele. :)  What's 
the best way to tell if a monster is one of these special monsters ---
is_covetous() for shopkeepers and
(mptr->geno & G_UNIQ) || mptr->msound == MS_GUARDIAN) for others, as in 
trap.c's animate_statue()?  Are there rings besides teleportation and 
invisibility that some monsters shouldn't ever put on?

   (3) What should happen when the player polymorphs into a purple worm
and digests a monster wearing a ring of foo? Is there any precedent in
the code for this situation? (I don't think so. Digesting an "oLS uses
it up, and digesting an "oR or speed boots does nothing, AFAICT.)
I could make digesting a ring grant the intrinsic, though.

